+
+Unless required by applicable law or agreed to in writing, software
+distributed under the License is distributed on an "AS IS" BASIS,
+WITHOUT WARRANTIES OR CONDITIONS OF ANY KIND, either express or implied.
+See the License for the specific language governing permissions and
+limitations under the License.
+*/
+
+// Package checkpointselfheal lets the kubelet start when the CPU or memory
+// manager finds its checkpoint unusable, instead of exiting.
+//
+// Upstream refuses to start in that case and asks for the node to be drained
+// and the state file removed. This package does the second half: the affected
+// manager drops its state, and the containers whose assignments lived in it are
+// stopped so the normal lifecycle recreates them and pins them again.
+//
+// Two invariants hold the design together. Victims are collected before
+// anything is cleared, because afterwards the old assignments are gone. And
+// StopVictims runs inside containerManagerImpl.Start, before it returns: the
+// runtime is marked synced only afterwards, so no pod can be admitted while
+// CPUs and NUMA zones look free in the state but are still occupied.
+package checkpointselfheal
diff --git a/pkg/kubelet/cm/checkpointselfheal/metrics.go b/pkg/kubelet/cm/checkpointselfheal/metrics.go
